---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/legal.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Refund & Payments Policy - OTPWala"
  description="OTPWala's wallet top-up, order cancellation, service-credit, unauthorized-payment, and payment-dispute policy."
  canonical="https://otpwala.me/refund-policy"
>
  <div class="legal-page">
    <section class="legal-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="legal-hero-badge">
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 3-6.7"/><polyline points="3 3 3 9 9 9"/><path d="M12 7v5l3 2"/></svg>
          PAYMENTS & CREDITS
        </div>
        <h1>Refund & Payments Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-hero-sub">This policy explains how wallet deposits, order credits, payment errors, and unauthorized transactions are handled.</p>
        <div class="legal-meta">
          <span><strong>Effective Date:</strong> September 17, 2026</span>
          <span class="meta-dot">&middot;</span>
          <span><strong>Last Updated:</strong> September 17, 2026</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="container legal-body">
      <div class="legal-layout">
        <aside class="legal-sidebar hide-mobile">
          <div class="legal-toc">
            <h4>Contents</h4>
            <nav>
              <a href="#wallet">Wallet deposits</a>
              <a href="#orders">Order credits</a>
              <a href="#errors">Payment errors</a>
              <a href="#fraud">Unauthorized payments</a>
              <a href="#contact">Contact support</a>
            </nav>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <article class="legal-content">
          <section id="wallet" class="legal-section">
            <h2>1. Wallet Deposits & Cryptocurrency Policy</h2>
            <p>OTPWala operates on a prepaid balance model supporting dual-currency display (USD primary, INR secondary). Users deposit funds using authorized payment methods, including <strong>Binance Pay (Crypto / USDT)</strong> and <strong>Instant UPI (INR)</strong>. Clear conversion rates, minimum deposit limits, and payment instructions are presented before you initiate any top-up.</p>
            <p>A wallet balance is intended strictly for on-platform services (purchasing virtual telephone numbers and SMS activations) on the account that received the verified payment. Wallet funds are non-transferable between accounts and cannot be withdrawn or converted to fiat cash or external cryptocurrency.</p>
            <p><strong>Cryptocurrency & Binance Pay Irreversibility:</strong> Due to the decentralized and immutable nature of blockchain networks and digital asset transfers, all cryptocurrency transactions completed via Binance Pay (USDT) are strictly final and irreversible once transmitted. Cryptocurrency deposits cannot be cancelled, reversed on-chain, refunded in crypto, or cashed out to external bank accounts. After a top-up has been confirmed and credited to your wallet balance, it is final for on-platform use.</p>
            <p>This policy is subject to applicable law and any mandatory rights relating to unauthorized, duplicate, or incorrectly processed payments. We do not waive statutory rights that cannot legally be excluded.</p>
          </section>

          <section id="orders" class="legal-section highlight-box">
            <div class="box-tag"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/><path d="M4 12h16"/></svg> ORDER CREDITS</div>
            <h2>2. Failed Orders and Cancellation Credits</h2>
            <p>Order pricing is displayed before confirmation. Cancellation may be unavailable during the initial waiting period or when the upstream provider rejects the request. The dashboard shows the result of the cancellation request.</p>
            <p>Where an eligible order does not receive an OTP and the order expires or is successfully cancelled, the applicable order amount is credited back to the OTPWala wallet. This is an on-platform service credit, not a cash refund, and the displayed processing window is an estimate rather than a guarantee.</p>
          </section>

          <section id="errors" class="legal-section">
            <h2>3. Payment Errors and Corrections</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>For a missing or delayed top-up, contact support with your payment identifier: the 12-digit UTR / UPI reference (for UPI) or Binance Order ID / TxID transaction hash (for Binance Pay), along with the amount, timestamp, and registered account email.</li>
              <li>For a duplicate charge, incorrect amount, or technical network error, report it promptly so we can reconcile the payment records against our processor logs and correct the account balance where appropriate.</li>
              <li>Do not submit a reused reference number, fabricated Binance Order ID / TxID, edited screenshot, altered receipt, or payment made from an unauthorized account. Such activity is strictly treated as payment fraud and results in immediate account restriction.</li>
              <li>Never send a UPI PIN, card CVV, account password, cryptocurrency private key, wallet seed phrase, or Binance login credentials to support. OTPWala staff will never ask for private security credentials.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section id="fraud" class="legal-section">
            <h2>4. Unauthorized Payments and Disputes</h2>
            <p>If you believe a payment was unauthorized, contact your bank, payment gateway, or Binance Pay support immediately and notify <a href="mailto:support@otpwala.me">support@otpwala.me</a>. We may request reasonable transaction identifiers and logs needed to investigate, preserve records, and coordinate with the respective payment network.</p>
            <p>Knowingly false payment disputes, chargeback abuse, fabricated transaction hashes, false claims of completed crypto transfers, or attempts to obtain both a wallet credit and an external reversal will result in immediate permanent account termination, forfeiture of unverified credits, and reporting to relevant payment networks, exchanges, or law enforcement authorities. Legitimate dispute rights remain unaffected.</p>
          </section>

          <section id="contact" class="legal-section">
            <h2>5. Contact Support</h2>
            <div class="contact-card">
              <strong>Payments Support</strong><br/>
              <span>Email:</span> <a href="mailto:support@otpwala.me">support@otpwala.me</a><br/>
              <span>Telegram:</span> <a href="https://t.me/OTPWalaSupport" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@OTPWalaSupport</a>
            </div>
            <p>See the <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> and <a href="/acceptable-use">Acceptable Use & Anti-Fraud Policy</a> for the full rules governing accounts and prohibited conduct.</p>
          </section>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
